        "custom_liquid": "<style>\n.article-template__title  {\n  font: 400 26px / 30px \"GoudyOldStyle\", serif !important;\n  text-transform: none;\n}\n#MainContent h5{\n  margin-bottom: 0px;\n}\n#MainContent h6 em,\n#MainContent h6{\n    font-family: 'Nexa', sans-serif !important;\n    font-size: calc(var(--font-heading-scale) * 1.3rem);\n    line-height: 1.3em;\n    text-transform: none;\nmargin-top: 0px;\n}\n\n/* Back link in Nexa at every width. The main section's custom_css styles every\n   `a` inside it as GoudyOldStyle with !important; this carries one more class\n   so it wins on specificity, and it targets only the back link so inline links\n   in the article body keep the prose face. */\n#MainContent .article-template__back-link {\n  font-family: \"Nexa\", sans-serif !important;\n}\n\n@media screen and (max-width: 749px) {\n  .article-template__title {\n    font: 400 20px / 25px \"GoudyOldStyle\", serif !important;\n  }\n  #MainContent .article-template__back-link {\n    font: 400 1.4rem / 25px \"Nexa\", sans-serif !important;\n  }\n}\n\n/* Optical centring for the back arrow.\n\n   Measured with canvas TextMetrics against the label's real cap band, not an\n   assumed ratio: the label is uppercase, so its visible centre sits well above\n   its line box centre and the arrow reads low.\n\n   Nudged with position/top rather than a bottom margin. A margin does not move\n   the arrow at all, it grows the flex line and pushes the label down, which\n   also changes the link's height. `top` moves the arrow itself and leaves\n   layout alone.\n\n   Measured uncorrected: arrow 1.39px low at 390, 2.09px low at 1440. The\n   offsets below land both within 0.1px of the cap centre. They are not the same\n   fraction of the font size, hence two values. */\n.article-template__back-link .icon-wrap {\n  display: flex;\n  transform: rotate(180deg);\n  width: 1.2rem;\n  height: 1.2rem;\n  position: relative;\n  top: -0.15rem;\n}\n\n@media screen and (min-width: 750px) {\n  .article-template__back-link .icon-wrap {\n    top: -0.2rem;\n  }\n}\n</style>",
